  "articleBody": "Replacing a bathroom vanity involves more than removing a cabinet: the new unit must fit the room, align with existing plumbing, accommodate the sink and countertop, and leave usable clearances. A professional assessment also helps identify water damage, outdated shutoffs, electrical conflicts, and permit questions before installation begins.",
